WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.982
A tuple is another ordered collection, but it is designed for values that should stay together and not be changed

00:00:07.982 --> 00:00:13.317
casually. The example stores latitude and longitude as one location tuple.

00:00:13.317 --> 00:00:17.787
Python can then unpack those two values into separate variables.

00:00:18.237 --> 00:00:24.134
This works nicely for fixed records such as coordinates, a pair of summary statistics,

00:00:24.134 --> 00:00:27.174
or several results returned from a function.

00:00:27.174 --> 00:00:32.462
The tuple still supports indexing, so position zero gives the latitude.
